          },
          "urpx:forRatePlanModifier": {
            "@id": "jemc:nm"
          },
          "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
            "@id": "jemc:cc-nm-2022-01-01",
            "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
            "urpx:completenessResult": {
              "@id": "urpx:partial"
            },
            "urpx:selfContained": true,
            "urpx:explainedBy": {
              "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
              "@id": "jemc:cc-nm-2022-01-01-evaluation",
              "urpx:evaluationKind": {
                "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
              },
              "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 5 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Avoided Energy Cost. Excess generation is credited at the Avoided Energy Cost, a formula of the base charge at the generator and transmission and distribution line losses for which the Cooperative publishes no value. The JSON-LD defines the credit as a per-kWh PriceDefinition with no Price, so a modeled bill credits nothing for excess generation. (2) Netting over the billing period. The rider compares the customer's generation with its consumption and credits only the excess; the JSON-LD carries the credit on exported kWh as metered, without stating over what interval generation and consumption are netted. (3) Credit balance and December payout. A credit balance is applied to the next month's bill, and each December any credit balance is paid to the customer by check. The JSON-LD carries no balance across bills. (4) Qualifying facilities. The facility must be solar photovoltaic, fuel cell or wind generation, owned and operated by the customer on its premises, operating in parallel with the Cooperative's system, intended primarily to offset the customer's own requirement, connected after January 1, 2016 and of not more than 10 kW for residential applications. URPX v0.5.1 has no fuel cell urpx:DERTypeValue, so the EligibilityRule carries residential customer kind and a solar or wind distributed energy resource; a fuel cell and the other conditions are in its description only. (5) Interconnection and additional purchases. The customer bears the costs of a safe interconnection under the Cooperative's Bulletin, and the Cooperative may purchase additional energy at a cost agreed with the customer. Neither is priced on the rider and neither is carried.",
              "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-18T00:00:00"
            }
          }
        }
      }
